WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:04.470
Film Courage: So I think aside from writing all of these scripts that you do and rewrites, you

00:00:04.470 --> 00:00:09.750
also do speaking engagements and you go to conferences?

00:00:09.750 --> 00:00:14.759
Christine Conradt, Screenwriter: I do. I speak a lot at conferences actually. And I do a lot of workshops, which are a lot of fun. I love

00:00:14.759 --> 00:00:20.609
teaching and so and then I also do
consulting when people hire me to read

00:00:20.609 --> 00:00:23.880
their scribes so I do that too which is
also great because it's also another

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:30.689
form of teaching when I do consulting
usually they obviously give me a feature

00:00:30.689 --> 00:00:34.890
that I'm giving notes on but it's really
not about notes for that particular

00:00:34.890 --> 00:00:37.860
scribe it's about teaching them how to
become better writers and so that's a

00:00:37.860 --> 00:00:40.739
lot of fun for me too
and so they can go to your website which

00:00:40.739 --> 00:00:45.480
will have underneath a video and yeah
the information is there yeah okay great

00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:50.160
let's say I'm a hypothetical person
attending one of these conferences and

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:53.399
then I'm one of the people waiting in
line to talk to you and you know just

00:00:53.399 --> 00:00:58.530
say hey really enjoy the information I
was wondering dot dot dot and that is

00:00:58.530 --> 00:01:04.049
how can I become a working writer so I
don't have to work a part-time job I

00:01:04.049 --> 00:01:10.590
just want to go right into it I think
that everybody's journey is so different

00:01:10.590 --> 00:01:14.729
in this business you know if you want to
become a doctor you go to med school you

00:01:14.729 --> 00:01:18.210
do your residency and you become a
doctor and you know you go work at a

00:01:18.210 --> 00:01:24.479
hospital that's not the way it works in
the film industry the key to success in

00:01:24.479 --> 00:01:28.140
the film industry is being opened
opportunities and being able to see them

00:01:28.140 --> 00:01:33.960
when they come everybody has sort of
this type A personality plan right where

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:38.280
we go okay so I want this by this date
and then I'm gonna try to do this and we

00:01:38.280 --> 00:01:42.030
think of that as being ambitious right
that we have a plan we're working toward

00:01:42.030 --> 00:01:45.750
something and there's absolutely nothing
wrong with that but if you get too

00:01:45.750 --> 00:01:49.829
obsessed with that so much so that you
don't see opportunities that come to you

00:01:49.829 --> 00:01:54.960
that may not fall in that plan you can
miss out on a lot of opportunities and

00:01:54.960 --> 00:02:02.369
so like I tell this story I've told it
before when I was in film school a

00:02:02.369 --> 00:02:06.090
friend of mine does Amba movies and
there's only five girls in my class and

00:02:06.090 --> 00:02:09.060
so I was always a zombie and one of his
movies because he had no one else to

00:02:09.060 --> 00:02:15.510
choose from Anna years later
we were graduated and he's a real

00:02:15.510 --> 00:02:17.790
producer and he calls me up he's like
hey Christine I'm doing a real zombie

00:02:17.790 --> 00:02:21.840
movie do you want to come down and be a
zombie just for old times sake and I was

00:02:21.840 --> 00:02:26.910
like sure I'll come down for one day and
so I go down and I'm sitting there and

00:02:26.910 --> 00:02:31.350
I'm in full zombie makeup like my hair
is he's out I'm green and I'm sitting

00:02:31.350 --> 00:02:34.500
there with the background and if you've
ever been on a film set you know that

00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:37.610
you know background it's pretty boring
you're sitting around most the time and

00:02:37.610 --> 00:02:42.210
but it's fun and it's a great day off
and as I was sitting there I meet this

00:02:42.210 --> 00:02:47.130
guy also a zombie who had just arrived
from from Boston and he had gotten a

00:02:47.130 --> 00:02:52.230
part on an HBO series called Carnivale
this is actually several years ago and

00:02:52.230 --> 00:02:57.600
we started talking and he tells me that
he has the rights to the soft Broadway

00:02:57.600 --> 00:03:01.950
play and he's looking for someone to
adapt it so at the end of the day he was

00:03:01.950 --> 00:03:05.880
a cool guy really nice I tell him well
you know if you need someone to adapt

00:03:05.880 --> 00:03:10.530
that into a screenplay for you let me
know and then the very next day the

00:03:10.530 --> 00:03:14.670
director calls me it was like I heard
you're adapting our off-broadway play

00:03:14.670 --> 00:03:19.560
and just was like oh yeah I did commit
to that yesterday but sure so well let's

00:03:19.560 --> 00:03:22.980
meet and talk about it
so I go to meet with him and the

00:03:22.980 --> 00:03:27.450
director and this guy and I realized
when I get to the coffee shop we're

00:03:27.450 --> 00:03:29.760
gonna meet I don't know what they look
like because we were all dressed as

00:03:29.760 --> 00:03:34.470
zombies and so I have no clue what they
even look like so we finally find each

00:03:34.470 --> 00:03:41.220
other and we end up doing a short and
that short premiere at the LA Latino

00:03:41.220 --> 00:03:47.250
Film Festival and that was great it was
a great experience I got to walk the red

00:03:47.250 --> 00:03:51.840
carpet wonderful I just did it to be
nice right after just doing something to

00:03:51.840 --> 00:03:57.330
be nice for my friend from college a
year later I get a call from them and

00:03:57.330 --> 00:04:02.400
they're like you know what Christine we
have some good news based on the short

00:04:02.400 --> 00:04:05.010
that we did
we've got financing to make the feature

00:04:05.010 --> 00:04:11.100
do you want to write the screenplay for
$25,000 and I mean yeah of course no I'm

00:04:11.100 --> 00:04:14.489
gonna say no to 25 grand so especially
when I was still in debt and all and

00:04:14.489 --> 00:04:18.270
this was during that that period of five
years where you know I was just doing

00:04:18.270 --> 00:04:25.470
things to be on film sets and to network
and so yeah I did that and again that

00:04:25.470 --> 00:04:28.360
was an opportunity
very still very proud of a film that

00:04:28.360 --> 00:04:33.910
film became Hotel California starring
Tatyana Ali had a great cast it

00:04:33.910 --> 00:04:40.360
premiered the following year so 2 years
later as a feature at the LA Latino Film

00:04:40.360 --> 00:04:47.590
Festival and did very well so again you
have to be open to opportunities I never

00:04:47.590 --> 00:04:53.290
went in to playing a zombie thinking I'm
gonna meet somebody who's going to have

00:04:53.290 --> 00:04:56.410
me write a short that we're gonna then
turn into a future it doesn't work out

00:04:56.410 --> 00:05:02.580
that way just make yourself available
and try to meet the right people and

00:05:02.580 --> 00:05:07.510
create situations where people owe you
favors and they want to work with you

00:05:07.510 --> 00:05:11.410
again and when you can do that then
those opportunities will start to come

00:05:11.410 --> 00:05:16.360
but you've got to be able to recognize
them when they happen that's a great

00:05:16.360 --> 00:05:19.870
story I feel like we're in this sort of
like hacking bubble where everybody's

00:05:19.870 --> 00:05:23.410
got it wants to try to like make this
quicker and make that quicker and if I

00:05:23.410 --> 00:05:27.400
follow this person on social media they
might they might just put me in the

00:05:27.400 --> 00:05:32.680
project which it all happens I know that
it does but I feel like we were in this

00:05:32.680 --> 00:05:37.570
new era of everything's got to be
quicker and it sounds like you although

00:05:37.570 --> 00:05:41.020
I'm sure you wanted certain things to go
faster you did things a little bit of a

00:05:41.020 --> 00:05:46.290
different way but I think a lot of it
was I never went into all of that

00:05:46.290 --> 00:05:48.460
thinking that there was gonna be some
payoff

00:05:48.460 --> 00:05:55.630
I just loved being on film sets I loved
meeting other filmmakers I loved taking

00:05:55.630 --> 00:06:02.680
an off-broadway play and adapting I'd
never done that before and so for me it

00:06:02.680 --> 00:06:10.330
was more about the love of doing those
things rather than the payoff of somehow

00:06:10.330 --> 00:06:14.830
I can I can turn this into a moneymaker
for me or somehow I can make this turn

00:06:14.830 --> 00:06:19.530
this into a rung in my career it was
never ever like that so you know the

00:06:19.530 --> 00:06:23.530
Deepak Chopra says you know we make
every decision based on love or fear

00:06:23.530 --> 00:06:30.790
right so all of those decisions when I
look back now I know we're based on the

00:06:30.790 --> 00:06:36.370
love of writing and the love of becoming
a screenwriter not the fear of am I

00:06:36.370 --> 00:06:39.370
wasting my time helping this person when
I should be helping that person because

00:06:39.370 --> 00:06:41.919
they're gonna
pay me quicker they're gonna get me into

00:06:41.919 --> 00:06:47.770
their movie or they're gonna do this it
was never like that for me right I like

00:06:47.770 --> 00:06:51.069
this your intention was different it
wasn't about what were you gonna get

00:06:51.069 --> 00:06:54.460
right and when you're not looking at
what the pay when you're not trying to

00:06:54.460 --> 00:06:59.020
see what the payoff is down the line
there's no there's a disappointment in

00:06:59.020 --> 00:07:02.169
it when the payoff doesn't come because
you're open to whatever that's gonna

00:07:02.169 --> 00:07:06.909
lead you to next right and so your since
you're quoting Deepak Chopra I'm gonna

00:07:06.909 --> 00:07:11.319
quote Louise hey since we're going there
and her thing that I love that she would

00:07:11.319 --> 00:07:14.770
say was well that's not a million
dollars and people stop on it and walk

00:07:14.770 --> 00:07:20.080
away from it because again we're so
we're looking for you know I mean I'm

00:07:20.080 --> 00:07:23.080
sure everybody would love to walk the
red carpet but it took these little

00:07:23.080 --> 00:07:27.550
steps it took you going to the set it
took you talking to this guy it you know

00:07:27.550 --> 00:07:31.629
it forming a relationship a business
relationship and then then that happened

00:07:31.629 --> 00:07:35.529
but people just see that result of oh
she's on the right carpet a that I want

00:07:35.529 --> 00:07:39.759
to be there exactly and they don't
really know what it takes to get there

00:07:39.759 --> 00:07:44.589
and and that's why again you have to be
so careful about letting yourself become

00:07:44.589 --> 00:07:48.279
resentful like looking at other people
and where they are and saying why can't

00:07:48.279 --> 00:07:54.639
I get there why can I get there
that energy is not well spent so focus

00:07:54.639 --> 00:08:00.909
on why are you writing if your goal and
just honestly be honest with yourself if

00:08:00.909 --> 00:08:06.960
your goal is to make money if your goal
is to be famous if your goal is to be

00:08:06.960 --> 00:08:13.710
recognizable and have a name then this
may not be the career for you because

00:08:13.710 --> 00:08:19.569
there there are easier ways to get those
things than by being a screenwriter so I

00:08:19.569 --> 00:08:24.000
think if you just can say I love writing
I want to see what today brings and

00:08:24.000 --> 00:08:27.669
enjoy every moment that you get to be on
set you get to be talking to directors

00:08:27.669 --> 00:08:32.949
whatever you're doing you know these
writing conferences are a great example

00:08:32.949 --> 00:08:37.149
when you go to these writing conferences
people are there because they just love

00:08:37.149 --> 00:08:41.409
to write they're just soaking it in and
it's such a creative inspiring

00:08:41.409 --> 00:08:46.959
environment spend your time doing those
things right and take every piece of

00:08:46.959 --> 00:08:52.110
information that you can and and learn
and become better at what you do because

00:08:52.110 --> 00:08:57.279
the gratification that you
from becoming really good and writing

00:08:57.279 --> 00:09:03.370
something and saying wow this is pretty
amazing that I mean nothing compares to

00:09:03.370 --> 00:09:07.779
that not walking a red carpet not seeing
your name on television nothing compares

00:09:07.779 --> 00:09:10.470
to that feeling

00:09:16.540 --> 00:09:18.600
you

